WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:04.879
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:04.880 --> 00:08.174
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:08.175 --> 00:12.011
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:12.012 --> 00:14.847
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:14.848 --> 00:18.184
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:18.185 --> 00:21.604
<i>Lucky there's a man
who positively can do</i>

00:21.605 --> 00:23.064
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:23.065 --> 00:24.690
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:24.691 --> 00:29.696
<i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy!</i>

00:37.537 --> 00:39.622
Oh, fun! Look, Peter.

00:39.623 --> 00:42.041
Smash Mouth is playing here
next weekend.

00:42.042 --> 00:44.543
- In Quahog?
- No, in this porn store.

00:44.544 --> 00:46.045
Well, you caught us.

00:46.046 --> 00:47.546
Lois and I are stocking up

00:47.547 --> 00:49.882
for a very special anniversary evening,

00:49.883 --> 00:52.134
and I'm not sure
that five percent discount

00:52.135 --> 00:53.928
was worth checking in here on Facebook.

00:55.222 --> 00:57.431
Ew, Meg, don't "like" that.

00:57.432 --> 00:59.767
Anyway, to celebrate,
we thought it would be fun

00:59.768 --> 01:03.646
to recount the three greatest
love stories ever told.

01:03.647 --> 01:06.274
We'll begin
with the tale of Helen of Troy:

01:06.275 --> 01:08.985
"The face that launched
a thousand ships."

01:08.986 --> 01:10.820
Which is the poetic way of saying,

01:10.821 --> 01:12.989
"Helen of Troy was thicc, tho."

01:12.990 --> 01:14.991
Which is the Black Twitter way
of saying,

01:14.992 --> 01:16.951
"She was very attractive."

01:24.626 --> 01:26.335
The people of Troy's chocolate

01:26.336 --> 01:27.920
has gotten into our peanut butter.

01:27.921 --> 01:29.630
The people of Greece's peanut butter

01:29.631 --> 01:31.382
has gotten all over our chocolate!

01:31.383 --> 01:33.509
We could perhaps try the combined taste,

01:33.510 --> 01:35.678
or we could fight to the death.

01:35.679 --> 01:38.472
Guys, stop! The Battle of
the Greece's Peanut Butter Cup

01:38.473 --> 01:39.890
has gone on too long.

01:39.891 --> 01:42.893
Let us agree to disagree.

01:42.894 --> 01:46.147
Huh, what a pleasantly
de-escalating phrase

01:46.148 --> 01:48.274
that I'm just now hearing
for the first time.

01:48.275 --> 01:50.818
Yes, we will agree to disagree.

01:50.819 --> 01:53.654
The war between the Greeks
and the Trojans is over!

01:54.823 --> 01:56.157
To Greece!

01:56.158 --> 01:59.201
Now let's go call a bunch
of jagged rocks a beach.

02:00.829 --> 02:02.330
- Ooh! Ow!
- Sharp! Sharp! Sharp!

02:02.331 --> 02:03.582
- Hot!
- Hot!

02:07.085 --> 02:08.794
Man, I'm happy the war is over.

02:08.795 --> 02:10.796
I can't wait to get back to Troy.

02:10.797 --> 02:12.715
Yeah, I'm just gonna plop down
with my kids

02:12.716 --> 02:14.593
<i>and watch Troy Story.</i>

02:14.594 --> 02:19.013
To the other side
of that hill... and beyond!

02:19.014 --> 02:22.350
That's as far as we know about
right now.

02:22.351 --> 02:23.651
You know what I just realized?

02:23.652 --> 02:26.896
This. This could be a really long poem.

02:26.897 --> 02:29.482
Now, if you'll excuse me,
Helen's in my cabin,

02:29.483 --> 02:32.943
and I thought I'd give
heterosexual sex a try.

02:34.237 --> 02:36.489
Helen?! What the Hades?!

02:36.490 --> 02:37.740
What? She's hot.

02:37.741 --> 02:39.492
But not as hot as Medusa.

02:39.493 --> 02:42.661
Ah, one look at Medusa,
and I'm rock hard.

02:42.662 --> 02:45.165
Mythologically correct.

02:48.335 --> 02:51.754
Coming up, Greek food voted
burpiest in the world.

02:51.755 --> 02:53.839
But first, in tragedy news:

02:53.840 --> 02:57.343
your queen, Helen, has run off
with Paris back to Troy.

02:57.344 --> 02:58.761
This is an outrage!

02:58.762 --> 03:02.264
I'll send my entire army after
them, led by my best warriors!

03:02.265 --> 03:04.684
Achilles, ACL, get in here!

03:09.689 --> 03:11.857
- What?
- Helen has run off with Paris!

03:11.858 --> 03:14.735
We're going to get her back
and burn Troy to the ground.

03:14.736 --> 03:16.070
Well, that sounds good.

03:16.071 --> 03:18.739
I just need to cancel my lesson
with Socrates first.

03:18.740 --> 03:21.033
Isn't he that thinker
they keep shuffling around

03:21.034 --> 03:22.868
from one philosophy school
district to the next?

03:22.869 --> 03:24.370
No, no, he's the one

03:24.371 --> 03:26.539
whose method is all about
asking questions.

03:26.540 --> 03:28.916
- Like what?
- "Have you ever tried wine?"

03:28.917 --> 03:30.126
"Can you keep a secret?"

03:30.127 --> 03:32.420
"You know this is your fault, right?"

03:32.421 --> 03:36.048
Yeah, he'll... he'll make you
question a lot about yourself.

03:41.179 --> 03:42.555
So, we'll sail directly east,

03:42.556 --> 03:45.099
and then head north
at a 90 degree angle.

03:45.100 --> 03:47.935
It's the fastest possible way
I can imagine getting there.

03:47.936 --> 03:49.603
Hang on. Let me see that.

03:49.604 --> 03:52.481
Pythagoras just invented this
thing called a "hypotenuse."

03:52.482 --> 03:55.401
If we know this distance
and this distance,

03:55.402 --> 03:58.070
we can calculate this more direct route.

03:58.071 --> 04:01.574
Wow. Our people are, like, really smart.

04:01.575 --> 04:03.451
I bet Greeks will always be known

04:03.452 --> 04:06.579
for their advancements in math
and not as cartoon characters

04:06.580 --> 04:10.082
with very hairy arms and
a tragically mismanaged economy.

04:19.843 --> 04:22.928
Okay, I had a feeling this
fortress would be impenetrable,

04:22.929 --> 04:25.431
so I've hired the finest builder
in Greece

04:25.432 --> 04:27.516
to make us a giant wooden horse.

04:27.517 --> 04:30.186
We'll hide inside it,
they'll take it in as a gift,

04:30.187 --> 04:32.605
and then we spring out
and destroy the city.

04:32.606 --> 04:34.440
I call it "the Trojan horse."

04:34.441 --> 04:35.941
Well, that sounds great,

04:35.942 --> 04:38.235
but there's another door
right here that's just beads.

04:38.236 --> 04:40.446
- What?
- Yeah. Just beads. See?

04:40.447 --> 04:42.781
Oh, boy, this...

04:42.782 --> 04:45.075
this is gonna be a difficult phone call.

04:45.076 --> 04:46.327
Let's go! Let's go!

04:46.328 --> 04:48.579
This needs to be done yesterday!

04:48.580 --> 04:49.872
Hello?

04:49.873 --> 04:51.999
Giant Horse Company, Pay On Delivery,

04:52.000 --> 04:53.959
No Deposit Required. Can I help you?

04:53.960 --> 04:55.419
What?!

05:05.472 --> 05:07.097
Where the hell is everyone?

05:07.098 --> 05:08.474
Well, they left a note.

05:08.475 --> 05:10.851
It says Helen and Paris went back

05:10.852 --> 05:13.312
to the Greek Isles to get married...

05:13.313 --> 05:16.982
And all three of Helen's fathers
are going to be there?!

05:16.983 --> 05:20.486
<i>Dancing queen...</i>

05:20.487 --> 05:21.904
They came!

05:21.905 --> 05:24.156
Awesome! And now
that we're owned by Disney,

05:24.157 --> 05:26.158
we can have Hercules here.

05:26.159 --> 05:27.826
No?

05:27.827 --> 05:29.328
They-they won't let us use him?

05:29.329 --> 05:31.664
What was the point of this whole merger?

05:31.665 --> 05:33.499
<i>Well, who can we use?</i>

05:33.500 --> 05:34.833
"Launchpad McQuack"?

05:34.834 --> 05:37.044
No. No. No, you know what?
I'm exhausted.

05:37.045 --> 05:39.338
I'm exhausted with being told "no."

05:39.339 --> 05:41.173
And now I'm married. Ugh.

05:41.174 --> 05:43.803
I'm gonna go break wieners off statues.

05:54.437 --> 05:57.898
Welcome back. My credit card
got declined at the sex store.

05:57.899 --> 06:00.067
We ran off with only the stuff
we could keister.

06:00.068 --> 06:03.112
<i>Our next love story is Romeo and Juliet,</i>

06:03.113 --> 06:06.198
a 500-year-old tale about horny preteens

06:06.199 --> 06:10.077
that society somehow decided
is classy and not perverted,

06:10.078 --> 06:13.831
even though two middle schoolers
bang in it. Enjoy.

06:13.832 --> 06:16.625
Two households, both alike in dignity,

06:16.626 --> 06:19.044
in fair Verona where we lay our scene.

06:19.045 --> 06:21.880
Well, I'd say Verona's better than fair.

06:21.881 --> 06:23.882
<i>They's gettin' a Shake Shack
this summer.</i>

06:23.883 --> 06:26.677
<i>Ooh, milkshakes and crinkly fries.</i>

06:26.678 --> 06:28.887
<i>Gonna have myself a pooch-belly
if I's not careful.</i>

06:28.888 --> 06:30.472
<i>I'm sorry, y'all.</i>

06:30.473 --> 06:33.559
<i>I done chatterboxed my way
through the whole prologue.</i>

06:33.560 --> 06:35.269
Boy, this is nice.

06:35.270 --> 06:37.896
Will there ever be
a more popular Italian city

06:37.897 --> 06:39.231
- than Verona?
- I don't know.

06:39.232 --> 06:41.609
<i>Are we even supposed
to be at this party?</i>

06:41.610 --> 06:44.612
If they find out we're Montagues,
they might razz us!

06:44.613 --> 06:46.405
Relax. No one's gonna recognize us.

06:46.406 --> 06:49.074
We got inch-wide masks
over just our eyes,

06:49.075 --> 06:51.118
with the rest of our faces
plainly visible.

06:51.119 --> 06:52.202
We're fine.

06:52.203 --> 06:54.204
You wanted to see me, Daddy?

06:54.205 --> 06:55.914
Juliet, honey, we need to talk.

06:55.915 --> 06:57.249
You're a grown woman now,

06:57.250 --> 06:59.293
and it's time for you to get married.

06:59.294 --> 07:01.295
Grown woman?! Daddy, I'm 13.

07:01.296 --> 07:04.306
Shh. Uh, don't say that.
Tell people you're 11!

07:04.307 --> 07:05.924
Do you want to get married or not?!

07:05.925 --> 07:07.468
Fine.

07:07.469 --> 07:09.094
Now, I found you
the most eligible bachelor

07:09.095 --> 07:11.055
in all of Italy.

07:11.056 --> 07:13.724
He's from the Boyardee family.
Kind of a big deal.

07:13.725 --> 07:17.936
My family makes the best canned
sugar pastas in all the land.

07:17.937 --> 07:19.938
Are you out of breath
from saying one sentence?

07:19.939 --> 07:21.649
Just give me a second.

07:21.650 --> 07:24.276
I'm in the midst of a full-on,
lockdown sodium headache.

07:24.277 --> 07:26.362
I haven't peed for 36 hours.

07:26.363 --> 07:28.113
Whew. Okay.

07:28.114 --> 07:31.700
Now, fair Juliet,
let our houses join together,

07:31.701 --> 07:34.662
like beef... and roni.

07:36.373 --> 07:37.540
Ah, cool!

07:43.838 --> 07:45.757
Shakespeare.

07:55.892 --> 07:57.810
What... what is that?

07:57.811 --> 07:59.311
It says "hole."

07:59.312 --> 08:00.729
I don't get it.

08:00.730 --> 08:01.897
You wrote "butt."

08:01.898 --> 08:03.219
Okay.

08:03.220 --> 08:04.692
I'll... I'll come over there.

08:06.027 --> 08:08.028
Hey, there's something
I want you to see.

08:08.029 --> 08:10.823
Some greaseball at the bar
just drew a guy in a circle.

08:10.824 --> 08:13.992
It's amazing. He's this,
and then he's this.

08:13.993 --> 08:16.741
You-you just...
y-you got to come see it!

08:17.831 --> 08:20.332
Romeo, we got to get out of here!

08:20.333 --> 08:23.335
Tybalt found out we're
Montagues, and he's pissed.

08:23.336 --> 08:25.921
Oh, man, I-I must have amnesia
or something,

08:25.922 --> 08:28.257
'cause I don't (BLEEP) remember
inviting you guys.

08:28.258 --> 08:31.009
- Who are you here with?
- Uh... Tony?

08:31.010 --> 08:32.678
Gonna have to do better than that, man.

08:32.679 --> 08:33.887
Lot of Tonys here.

08:33.888 --> 08:35.389
Oh, did I say "Tony"?

08:35.390 --> 08:39.727
I-I meant... I'm Abe Froman,
the sausage king of Chicago.

08:39.728 --> 08:42.521
<i>You're Abe Froman,
the sausage king of Chicago?</i>

08:42.522 --> 08:43.731
That's right.

08:43.732 --> 08:46.066
Hello?

08:46.067 --> 08:47.901
<i>Yes, I'm looking for Abe Froman,</i>

08:47.902 --> 08:49.695
<i>the sausage king of Chicago.</i>

08:49.696 --> 08:51.113
<i>Heavyset fellow, glasses.</i>

08:51.114 --> 08:52.906
Oh, w-well, he's right here.

08:52.907 --> 08:54.199
Let me just... Wait a minute!

08:54.200 --> 08:56.201
We don't have phones or Chicago!

08:56.202 --> 08:57.703
All right, you got to die.

08:57.704 --> 08:59.955
Enough! You three, out of my house!

08:59.956 --> 09:02.833
I will not play host
to some family feud!

09:06.004 --> 09:07.588
100 people surveyed.

09:07.589 --> 09:09.256
Top five answers are on the board.

09:09.257 --> 09:12.050
Name something you might
say to a damned spot.

09:13.052 --> 09:14.595
Out.

09:14.596 --> 09:15.929
- Good answer! Good answer!
- Ah, good answer, good answer.

09:15.930 --> 09:18.098
- Yeah, yeah, good answer.
- Show me "out"!

09:19.476 --> 09:21.310
What?! That's impossible!

09:21.311 --> 09:24.396
Romeo, name something
you might say to a damned spot.

09:24.397 --> 09:25.773
Hello.

09:27.066 --> 09:29.193
- What?!
- I know this audience.

09:29.194 --> 09:32.030
- Of course it was "hello."
- Of course it was.

09:44.167 --> 09:45.584
Romeo?

09:45.585 --> 09:47.795
Juliet.

09:47.796 --> 09:49.505
I know I ain't supposed to be here,

09:49.506 --> 09:51.381
but I just had to see you again.

09:51.382 --> 09:55.803
Oh, Romeo, Romeo,
wherefore art thou, Romeo?

09:55.804 --> 09:57.513
I... What-what...
what are you talking about?

09:57.514 --> 09:59.181
I'm right here.
You're looking right at me.

09:59.182 --> 10:01.517
You know what? I'll come up there.

10:01.518 --> 10:03.101
Romeo, we can't.

10:03.102 --> 10:04.978
What if my father sees us?

10:04.979 --> 10:07.606
And "wherefore" means "why,"
by the way, not "where."

10:07.607 --> 10:08.982
Shh, shh, shh, shh.

10:08.983 --> 10:10.526
That's stupid. You're stupid.

10:10.527 --> 10:12.820
Juliet, I know we just met,

10:12.821 --> 10:15.989
but when I look at you,
I feel something special.

10:15.990 --> 10:19.618
This is gonna sound crazy,
but... will you marry me?

10:19.619 --> 10:22.329
Okay, let's do it.

10:22.330 --> 10:24.081
I love you, Romeo.

10:24.082 --> 10:25.999
I love you, too, Juliet.

10:28.837 --> 10:30.629
I should probably let you know

10:30.630 --> 10:32.798
I have a lot
of Jack Skellington tattoos.

10:32.799 --> 10:35.175
Well, I wish you would have
told me that before,

10:35.176 --> 10:39.137
but that's okay, because I do
karate outside against no one.

10:39.138 --> 10:43.142
Yeah, this is gonna be a good marriage.

10:48.231 --> 10:50.065
There he is!

10:50.066 --> 10:52.276
There's the dumb-ass
I've been looking for.

10:54.237 --> 10:55.362
Mercutio!

10:55.363 --> 10:57.739
I could never say this

10:57.740 --> 11:00.075
when I was alive, but...

11:00.076 --> 11:03.328
"Ralph... Fiennes."

11:10.169 --> 11:12.421
Oh, God.

11:12.422 --> 11:15.632
I'm voiding my bowels right now
because I died,

11:15.633 --> 11:18.886
not 30 minutes ago
in the carriage on the way here.

11:23.016 --> 11:26.059
Welp, we all know how this goes.

11:27.103 --> 11:28.771
I'm doin' it!

11:32.400 --> 11:33.859
Oh, Friar Laurence,

11:33.860 --> 11:36.778
are you absolutely sure faking my death

11:36.779 --> 11:38.530
with this poison is the best plan?

11:38.531 --> 11:41.533
Well, there's also Herbalife,
which is an amazing product.

11:41.534 --> 11:42.868
And I think you, specifically,

11:42.869 --> 11:44.870
would make a great addition to our team.

11:44.871 --> 11:47.039
I-I'll take the poison.
Thank you, Friar.

11:47.040 --> 11:49.374
A-And since I'm picking up
a prescription,

11:49.375 --> 11:52.252
can I, uh, pay
for the rest of my items here?

11:52.253 --> 11:54.963
Uh, I-I guess.

11:57.050 --> 11:59.302
Oh, yourself.

12:03.723 --> 12:05.557
I'm afraid she's dead.

12:05.558 --> 12:07.434
You can tell by her shallow breathing

12:07.435 --> 12:09.144
and weak but clear heartbeat.

12:09.145 --> 12:11.688
I'm sorry. There's nothing I can do.

12:11.689 --> 12:13.065
Can you make a paper airplane?

12:13.066 --> 12:16.027
- I can.
- Then don't be so hard on yourself.

12:20.490 --> 12:23.505
Oh, no! My girlfriend's dead!

12:23.506 --> 12:26.078
And on top of that,
it's that time in late summer

12:26.079 --> 12:28.747
before football starts
and there's no basketball.

12:28.748 --> 12:31.249
I mean, there is baseball,
but it's not playoffs.

12:31.250 --> 12:34.087
I might as well just be dead!

12:40.009 --> 12:42.010
Children having sex,

12:42.011 --> 12:43.345
two murders,

12:43.346 --> 12:45.514
double suicide.

12:45.515 --> 12:48.600
Very irresponsible to teach this...

12:48.601 --> 12:50.018
in schools.

12:51.354 --> 12:54.606
Romeo? Romeo?

12:54.607 --> 12:56.149
Oh, wherefore?

12:56.150 --> 12:58.777
- Stupid.
- I don't understand.

12:58.778 --> 13:00.445
We had a plan!

13:00.446 --> 13:03.949
Did you think I was dead just
because I faked my own death?!

13:03.950 --> 13:05.993
Maybe there's still poison on your lips.

13:05.994 --> 13:07.953
Mm. Alas.

13:07.954 --> 13:10.789
Just Costco hot dog.

13:10.790 --> 13:14.318
Well, a boy I knew
for three days is dead.

13:14.319 --> 13:17.045
And on top of that, WNBA season is over,

13:17.046 --> 13:20.298
and it's still two months
till figure skating starts!

13:26.667 --> 13:31.226
<i>For never was a story of more "Oh, no!"</i>

13:31.227 --> 13:34.731
<i>than that of Juliet and her Romeo.</i>

13:41.404 --> 13:43.363
I accidentally farted on a candle

13:43.364 --> 13:46.199
<i>at our Eyes Wide Shut party
and this happened.</i>

13:46.200 --> 13:48.660
<i>Now, please enjoy Fatal Attraction.</i>

13:55.251 --> 13:57.836
Man, is this a great
black toilet loft party or what?

13:57.837 --> 13:59.212
Oh, yeah.

13:59.213 --> 14:01.591
Hey, which line of cocaine
is for the bathroom?

14:01.592 --> 14:04.009
- I think it's that one.
- Thanks. I'll be right back.

14:07.889 --> 14:10.348
Dan Gallagher. Confident to meet you.

14:10.349 --> 14:13.060
I'm not gonna be ignored by you, Dan.

14:13.061 --> 14:14.686
No, no. No, no, that's later.

14:14.687 --> 14:16.855
Would you like to dance in silence,

14:16.856 --> 14:19.066
because they always add
the music in post?

14:19.067 --> 14:20.735
Sure.

14:21.778 --> 14:23.695
What do you think they'll choose?

14:23.696 --> 14:25.280
<i>You take the good, you take the bad</i>

14:25.281 --> 14:27.240
<i>You take 'em both and there you have</i>

14:27.241 --> 14:30.453
<i>The facts of life, the facts of life.</i>

14:34.916 --> 14:37.042
Now, let's have hot sex in silence,

14:37.043 --> 14:39.544
and they'll add
the sensuous music in post.

14:43.883 --> 14:46.468
I wonder what music they're gonna add.

14:47.887 --> 14:49.387
<i>Inspector Gadget</i>

14:49.388 --> 14:50.890
<i>Hoo, hoo</i>

14:52.141 --> 14:53.141
<i>Inspector Gadget</i>

14:53.142 --> 14:54.559
Well, I'm done.

14:59.232 --> 15:01.025
<i>Inspector Gadget</i>

15:02.068 --> 15:03.318
<i>Hoo, hoo...</i>

15:03.319 --> 15:06.363
TV themes were longer back now.

15:09.867 --> 15:11.166
I love our life.

15:11.167 --> 15:12.744
Yeah. It's hard not to root

15:12.745 --> 15:15.080
for a rich, white lawyer
in the Connecticut suburbs.

15:16.124 --> 15:18.416
Dad, the not cell phone's ringing!

15:18.417 --> 15:20.502
Let's let the new
answering machine get it.

15:20.503 --> 15:22.796
<i>Hi, you've reached the Gallaghers.</i>

15:22.797 --> 15:24.798
<i>Leave a message for our intact family</i>

15:24.799 --> 15:26.424
<i>after the beep.</i>

15:26.425 --> 15:28.468
<i>Hi, Dan. It's Alex Forrest.</i>

15:28.469 --> 15:31.148
<i>I just found out I'm preg...</i>

15:31.149 --> 15:33.515
<i>Now I'm giving you a minute
to pick up the phone hastily.</i>

15:33.516 --> 15:35.016
I got it, I got it, I got it! Hello?

15:35.017 --> 15:37.477
Judge Forrest.:
How did you get this number

15:37.478 --> 15:39.980
when they deliver a book
that has all the numbers?

15:39.981 --> 15:43.942
Dan, look over to the split
screen and see how crazy I look.

15:43.943 --> 15:46.111
- Eesh.
- And, also,

15:46.112 --> 15:47.445
I'm listening to opera,

15:47.446 --> 15:48.822
but I don't know which one,

15:48.823 --> 15:50.365
'cause they'll add it in post.

15:50.366 --> 15:52.242
What do you think they'll choose?

15:52.243 --> 15:56.746
<i>No more Rice Krispies</i>

15:56.747 --> 16:00.334
<i>We ran out of Rice Krispies...</i>

16:04.630 --> 16:06.173
I see it!

16:06.174 --> 16:07.592
God!

16:11.095 --> 16:14.056
Hello, Dan.

16:15.349 --> 16:16.725
How did you get in here?

16:16.726 --> 16:20.312
I slipped the security guard
five cocaines.

16:20.313 --> 16:21.855
I told you it's over!

16:21.856 --> 16:24.191
And I told you we need to talk.

16:24.192 --> 16:25.817
I'm pregnant.

16:25.818 --> 16:27.420
Are you sure it's yours?

16:27.421 --> 16:29.321
- I am.
- We can get rid of it.

16:29.322 --> 16:31.865
They won't outlaw abortion until 2019.

16:31.866 --> 16:33.408
No, I'm keeping it!

16:33.409 --> 16:35.035
And one other thing:

16:35.036 --> 16:38.580
<i>the baby will not be ignored
by you, Dan.</i>

16:38.581 --> 16:41.209
That's a very big thing for you,
isn't it?

16:44.962 --> 16:46.213
I need your help.

16:46.214 --> 16:47.923
Alex, the elevator chick, is pregnant.

16:47.924 --> 16:49.507
I don't want to lose my family.

16:49.508 --> 16:50.717
What can I do?

16:50.718 --> 16:51.843
Listen, just call your wife

16:51.844 --> 16:53.678
on your numbers-on-the-top car phone,

16:53.679 --> 16:55.055
and it'll all be better.

16:55.056 --> 16:56.890
If I were you, Dan, I'd just go home

16:56.891 --> 16:58.558
and enjoy your family and rabbit.

16:58.559 --> 17:00.853
Most of these things just boil over.

17:08.861 --> 17:10.070
That's odd.

17:10.071 --> 17:12.870
Usually, our rabbit rushes up
to greet me.

17:12.871 --> 17:15.742
Well, time to wash dishes
while looking at a lawn,

17:15.743 --> 17:17.494
like most housewives.

17:18.746 --> 17:21.159
What in the world?

17:21.160 --> 17:23.583
I better warily approach
that pot in silence,

17:23.584 --> 17:26.211
knowing they'll add
dramatic music in post.

17:26.212 --> 17:28.797
I wonder what they'll choose.

17:28.798 --> 17:33.468
<i>No more Rice Krispies</i>

17:33.469 --> 17:38.014
<i>We ran out of Rice Krispies!</i>

17:41.769 --> 17:44.730
Aw, I was going to kill the rabbit.

17:47.982 --> 17:50.068
All right, listen, Beth,

17:50.069 --> 17:52.671
I got something to tell you
in front of our kid.

17:52.672 --> 17:54.990
- I had an affair.
- You what?!

17:54.991 --> 17:57.027
I know. It was awesome at the time,

17:57.028 --> 17:59.229
and, frankly, I was real close
to getting away with it.

17:59.230 --> 18:01.503
But now that there are
actual consequences,

18:01.504 --> 18:04.749
- I got to tell you the truth.
- Dan, how could you?

18:04.750 --> 18:06.251
Look, it's not my fault.

18:06.252 --> 18:08.628
My plan was to just hide this
from you forever.

18:08.629 --> 18:09.963
Also, she's pregnant.

18:09.964 --> 18:11.589
How is that possible?

18:11.590 --> 18:14.259
Well, when a man and a woman
like each other just a little

18:14.260 --> 18:15.260
and they get in an elevator...

18:15.261 --> 18:16.261
Oh, God!

18:16.262 --> 18:18.096
How could I be so blind?!

18:18.097 --> 18:20.381
I wouldn't be so hard
on yourself, honey.

18:20.382 --> 18:21.516
But I will say,

18:21.517 --> 18:24.811
<i>at least she had a pot
of something on the stove</i>

18:24.812 --> 18:26.564
when I came home.

18:46.042 --> 18:50.295
Well, now to defog this mirror
and see only myself.

18:51.881 --> 18:56.343
Now to fully close the mirror
and have no changes.

18:57.636 --> 18:59.179
I'm sorry, Beth.

18:59.180 --> 19:02.015
I have a fatal attraction
to your husband.

19:02.016 --> 19:04.489
Ah! She said it! That'll be in the
trailer.

19:04.490 --> 19:07.687
I'm gonna do to you
what I did to your bunny

19:07.688 --> 19:09.147
and your neighbor's cat

19:09.148 --> 19:12.151
because I went to
the wrong house the first time.

19:13.861 --> 19:17.155
I love relaxing here
with that dry ceiling.

19:17.156 --> 19:20.158
Huh. Wonder if the weather
called for living room rain.

19:20.159 --> 19:21.493
<i>Next up, Connecticut,</i>

19:21.494 --> 19:23.078
<i>your living room forecast:</i>

19:23.079 --> 19:25.205
<i>dry, dry, dry.</i>

19:25.206 --> 19:28.208
That can only mean one thing!

19:31.170 --> 19:32.879
Oh, my God.

19:32.880 --> 19:34.756
It's happening. It's happening.

19:34.757 --> 19:35.799
Dan, help!

19:35.800 --> 19:37.468
Right.

19:43.307 --> 19:44.933
You deserve to die,

19:44.934 --> 19:47.310
because the choices I made
are your fault!

19:57.738 --> 19:59.864
All right. She's mostly choked.

19:59.865 --> 20:02.785
Let's just sit on the floor
with our backs to the tub.

20:09.125 --> 20:12.419
It's just been revoked.

20:23.055 --> 20:24.806
Hi, I'm Chris Griffin.

20:24.807 --> 20:26.558
I didn't have a lot to do tonight.

20:26.559 --> 20:28.351
But they did say
they'd give me one minute

20:28.352 --> 20:31.062
at the end of the show
to share my favorite love story.

20:31.063 --> 20:33.440
Of course, I chose
the classic romantic tale

20:33.441 --> 20:35.900
of the love between a young man
and pastry,

20:35.901 --> 20:37.569
<i>American Pie.</i>

20:37.570 --> 20:39.779
The store was all out of apple,

20:39.780 --> 20:41.406
so this one is chicken pot,

20:41.407 --> 20:43.116
fresh from the oven.

20:43.117 --> 20:44.367
Here we go.

20:44.368 --> 20:47.287
Ow, the piping hot gravy!

20:47.288 --> 20:49.914
Oh! And one of the peas went inside!

20:49.915 --> 20:51.124
It's so burned,

20:51.125 --> 20:53.585
I can't tell what's chicken
and what's me!

20:53.586 --> 20:55.962
Oh, God! Not gonna stop though!

20:55.963 --> 20:58.006
Happy anniversary, Mom and Dad,

20:58.007 --> 20:59.966
from your teenage son

20:59.967 --> 21:03.846
getting busy with a 400-degree pot pie!